// B226 (2026-10-19) — rogueone: unattended-upgrades must never move the NVIDIA driver.
// Install: /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/51weyland-hold-nvidia (runbook model-serving-ollama.md § NVIDIA driver).
//
// WHY: on 2026-10-09 unattended-upgrades upgraded the userspace driver 595.91.07 -> 595.99.02 while the loaded kernel
// module stayed 595.91.07 until a reboot (2026-10-19) — nine days of silent drift. A driver update needs a reboot to
// take effect, and in between a restarted Ollama loads the new libraries against the old module and can lose the GPU,
// taking every local model — including the MLflow gateway's guardrail judge (fail-closed) — to CPU.
//
// rogueone boots ONE pinned kernel (GRUB_DEFAULT = 6.17.0-35) and its nvidia module is built by DKMS for it, so the
// only way the module and the driver drift apart is a driver package moving without a reboot. Holding these packages
// costs nothing the host runs: kernel security updates still install (other kernels, not booted), and every other
// package still updates. Driver updates become deliberate: upgrade, reboot, check (scripts/gpu_driver_drift.py).
//
// Entries are prefixes (the same matching as 50unattended-upgrades' examples): "nvidia-" covers nvidia-driver-*,
// nvidia-dkms-*, nvidia-utils-*, nvidia-kernel-common-*, nvidia-container-toolkit, …; the linux-modules-nvidia
// metas would otherwise pull a newer nvidia-kernel-common through their `>=` dependency.
Unattended-Upgrade::Package-Blacklist {
    "nvidia-";
    "libnvidia-";
    "xserver-xorg-video-nvidia-";
    "linux-modules-nvidia-";
};
